Fictional Band Name: Velvet Turnstile Error

Band Description
Velvet Turnstile Error is a five-member acoustic-electronic ensemble built around the principle that a bassoon note is not one event but a chain of reed, air, key, and body actions that can be distributed across a footwork groove.

Mara Kovács — bassoon, double-tonguing, register design, Tongue Chain architecture.
DeShawn Bell — footwork drums, short mono sub, False Double programming, arrangement cuts.
Nia Brooks — prepared clavinet, dead-note gapwork, harmonic checkpoints.
Tomasz Zieliński — damped snare, woodblock, acoustic transient replacement.
Elena Varga — contrabass recorder, low air field, sub-free counterweight.

There is no conventional frontperson. Mara supplies the articulation map; DeShawn fractures the machine rhythm around it; Nia fills only the narrowest harmonic gaps; Tomasz creates acoustic transients that can be mistaken for keywork; Elena restores low acoustic air when electronic sub disappears. Live versions vary because reed stiffness, embouchure, tongue position, key regulation, room humidity, and register choice alter the spacing between RELEASE, SPEAK, CLICK, and BODY.

